Figure 6 illustrates Nano-11's role in improving antigen targeting and retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) express the highest levels of CD86, a key costimulatory molecule. Panel B further characterizes OVA-containing MigDCs, identifying them predominantly as CD11b+ DCs and monocyte-derived dendritic cells. Panel C, using in vivo fluorescence imaging, demonstrates that Alexa Fluor 647-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) formulated with Nano-11 or aluminum hydroxide is retained at the injection site for a significantly longer duration compared to soluble OVA, supporting Nano-11's efficacy in sustained antigen delivery.